  "note": "Modules that compile with ZERO rustc errors. THE GATE. A module leaving this set is a regression attributable to one file; that is what an error TOTAL can never tell you, and why the total stopped being the ratchet.",
  "not_covered": "A module NOT listed here already fails to compile. It can get worse and nothing will notice. That is accepted deliberately -- a ratchet over a mostly-broken population carries no signal (50 new errors was a 1.6% rise against 3,072 and passed).",
  "may_only_grow": "min_modules is a floor. Shrinking the set takes two edits so it cannot happen quietly.",
  "record_with": "python3 scripts/compile_check.py --record-clean-set",
  "why_the_floor_dropped_2026-08-03": "227 -> 220. Adding rule coverage for Logger.*Log severity variants and IGPIOExtensions.Set/Unset/Blink (rulesdb/rules/register_dsl.json) resolved 565 previously-gapped static-call instances, but also unblocked 7 methods that were previously withheld ENTIRELY by that same gap -- so nothing had ever reached rustc for them. Emitting them exposed 5 independent, pre-existing emitter defects (bit-field name mismatches, an unqualified register-collection enum name, unmapped C# `null`, a bit-width mismatch in a generated callback signature, unmapped `StringBuilder`), none of them caused by the Logger/GPIO rule itself. Tracked in issue #64; the floor should climb back past 227 as each is fixed.",
  "min_modules": 220,
